":" # Example"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```rust"},{"DocComment":" // type inference is helping us here, the way `from_fn` knows how many"},{"DocComment":" // elements to produce is the length of array down there: only arrays of"},{"DocComment":" // equal lengths can be compared, so the const generic parameter `N` is"},{"DocComment":" // inferred to be 5, thus creating array of 5 elements."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let array = core::array::from_fn(|i| i);"},{"DocComment":" // indexes are:    0  1  2  3  4"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(array, [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let array2: [usize; 8] = core::array::from_fn(|i| i * 2);"},{"DocComment":" // indexes are:     0  1  2  3  4  5   6   7"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(array2, [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let bool_arr = core::array::from_fn::<_, 5, _>(|i| i % 2 == 0);"},{"DocComment":" // indexes are:       0     1      2     3      4"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(bool_arr, [true, false, true, false, true]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" You can also capture things, for example to create an array full of clones"},{"DocComment":" where you can't just use `[item; N]` because it's not `Copy`:"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let my_string: [String; 2] = std::array::from_fn(|i| format!(\"Hello {i}\"));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(my_string, [\"Hello 0\", \"Hello 1\"]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The array is generated in ascending index order, starting from the front"},{"DocComment":" and going towards the back, so you can use closures with mutable state:"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let mut state = 1;"},{"DocComment":" let a = std::array::from_fn(|_| { let x = state; state *= 2; x });"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a, [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null},"gene